From: Swift Linux <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the test suite when cross compiling

The suite cannot run anywhere but on the target: it imports the target's
AccountsService typelib, LD_PRELOADs a libmocklibc built for the target,
and loads libaccountsservice out of the build tree.

tests/meson.build decided this for itself by asking the build machine's
python whether it could import gi and dbusmock. That is a question about
the wrong machine, and while the answer was no the directory quietly did
nothing. Once host PyGObject was installed for an unrelated reason the
answer became yes, and configuring failed in the first thing the block
does:

    tests/meson.build:49:12: ERROR: Command
    `.../unittest_inspector.py .../test-libaccountsservice.py`
    failed with status 1.

that being unittest_inspector.py importing the test module to enumerate
its cases and hitting the target-only imports inside it.

Guarding the block was not enough. subproject('mocklibc') sits above it,
outside any condition, so the mock C library was still configured and
built - and it does not survive a compiler defaulting to C23:

    ../subprojects/mocklibc-1.0/src/netgroup-debug.c:25:3: error:
    implicit declaration of function 'print_indent'
    [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Skip the whole directory instead. Nothing outside it uses libmocklibc,
and nothing after subdir('tests') depends on anything it defines.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -233,7 +233,13 @@
   subdir('doc/libaccountsservice')
 endif
 
-subdir('tests')
+# The suite imports the target's AccountsService typelib, LD_PRELOADs a
+# libmocklibc built for the target and loads libaccountsservice out of the
+# build tree, so none of it can run on the build machine. Skipping the
+# directory also skips the mocklibc subproject it builds for that purpose.
+if not meson.is_cross_build()
+  subdir('tests')
+endif
 
 configure_file(
   output: 'config.h',
